TB710FU macOS 27.3: increase workqueue thread stack size from 512 KiB to 4 MiB.

Hardware evidence (pl85, com5_pl85_live.log):
- WindowServer pid=302 completed Submit #1..#5 on Adreno 750 hardware, then died
  with SIGBUS (status=0xa, reason 2:10) at NativeAdrenoMetal+0xe809b8 (inline
  Rust stack probe `ldr xzr, [sp]`) inside native_bridge_metal_open ->
  nmb_device_open -> metal2vulkan_runtime::device::create::Device::system_default_with.
- Crash registers: fp=0x16f229ce0, sp=0x16f1d3d80 (352 KiB frame), BT[11]
  fp=0x16f254be0, total stack depth 0x80e60 (515.6 KiB > 512 KiB). The final
  probe at 0x16f1d3d80 hit the 4 KiB VM_PROT_NONE workq stack guard page
  [0x16f1d3000..0x16f1d4000).
- Userspace _pthread_wqthread_setup computes stacksize dynamically from the
  kernel-supplied (self - stacklowaddr), and virtual stack pages are demand-paged
  and marked VM_BEHAVIOR_REUSABLE in workq_markfree_threadstack.

diff --git a/kern/kern_support.c b/kern/kern_support.c
